cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Open Document Skills (or the open-document-lib library), please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Open Document Skills: a stdlib-only native-ODF toolkit and agent skill set (ODT/ODP/ODS/ODG)"
abstract: >-
  Open Document Skills is a dependency-free Python toolkit for the four
  OpenDocument formats — text (ODT), presentation (ODP), spreadsheet (ODS) and
  graphics (ODG). The shared library is published to PyPI as
  open-document-lib; four agent "skills" (SKILL.md) let an LLM generate, edit
  (structure-preserving), validate, brand/theme, repair and convert ODF files
  locally, on an open ISO standard, without a proprietary office suite or a DOCX
  detour. Capabilities include scholarly authoring (footnotes, BibTeX/CSL-JSON
  citations, cross-references, MathML), named ranges, data validation and
  embedded charts, connectors and shape groups, RelaxNG validation, and PDF
  rendering with LibreOffice as an optional QA companion.
